  "id": "ips",
  "term": "IPS",
  "definition": "IPS refers to internalizing problems: a pattern in which distress is turned inward, leading to excessive inward emotional focus, difficulty regulating emotions, and symptoms such as anxiety, depression, and somatic complaints. In adolescents, these problems can begin from early anxiety or depression tendencies, are often hard for others to notice, and may continue over time.",
